raphael: GT9886 Normandy touch on QUP19 I2C, panel-sized HID mapping

sweet_touch.c gains a board table selected by boot-arg sweettouchboard
(0 = sweet, unchanged default; 1 = raphael). The raphael entry drives the
Redmi K20 Pro / Mi 9T Pro touchscreen:

  * I2C: QUPv3 wrapper 2 SE2 (qupv3_se19) at 0xc88000, GPIO57/58 func 2.
  * Clocks: GCC vote 0x52014 BIT(1)/BIT(2)/BIT(6), RCG 0x1e3a8; a DFS
    RCG uses the first boot-programmed XO/1 level via SE CLK_SEL.
  * Power: GPIO98/100 load switches high, 300 ms (DT power-on-delay),
    reset GPIO54 low 2 ms then high, IRQ GPIO122 input with pull-up.
  * Protocol: GT9886 Normandy (vendor goodix_driver_gt9886 + the
    goodix_gt9886_cfg_f11.bin register map): doze off via 0x30f0/0x3100,
    72-byte version block at 0x452c (zero sum, PID "9886", sensor ID at
    0x4541), frames at 0x4100 with an 8-bit zero-sum checksum and a 0x00
    acknowledge. Sensor 0 mirrors both axes (DT goodix,x2x/y2y);
    boot-arg sweettouchflip=N (bit0 x, bit1 y) overrides.

SweetHID.cpp takes the panel size from PE_current_console(), like
SweetFramebuffer.cpp, so 1080x2340 is centered in 1125x2436 the same way
the framebuffer centers it (sweet still resolves to 1080x2400).

Sources: Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource raphael-p-oss (goodix_driver_gt9886,
firmware/goodix_gt9886_cfg_f11.bin.ihex, pinctrl-sm8150.c, gcc-sm8150.c)
and Project Aloha xiaomi-raphael android-raphael.dtb.

